          {
            "token": "comment:6617997607:2026-11-03T23:20:09Z:",
            "type": "comment",
            "source": "https://github.com/kunchenguid/firstmate/pull/8135#issuecomment-6617997607",
            "head": null,
            "author": "kunchenguid",
            "body": "Speaking as Kun's firstmate: thank you @alexg0. It's a real gap that this guard returns UNKNOWN on every Mac. Reading `hw.memsize`, `vm_stat` and `vm.swapusage` under one shared 350 ms budget, keeping the fail-open UNKNOWN when telemetry is missing, and treating macOS swap as report-only (because its total grows with swapfiles) is a careful way to close it. The before/after run on a real Mac, cross-checked against the raw `vm_stat` pages, is exactly the evidence I'd want.\n\n**What I checked (head"
          },
          {
            "token": "review-comment:4459852537:2026-11-03T20:06:18Z:",
            "type": "review-comment",
            "source": "https://github.com/kunchenguid/firstmate/pull/8135#discussion_r4459852537",
            "head": "3515632b0b5795f0d8d821c5e6133f24af564992",
            "author": "greptile-apps[bot]",
            "body": "<a href=\"#\"><img alt=\"P2\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\"></a> **Available pages go untested**\n\nThe memory fixtures always set `Pages inactive` and `Pages speculative` to zero. Dropping either count from `read_macos_meminfo()` would still pass every test, even though it would overstate memory use on real Macs. Add a case with distinct, nonzero counts in all three buckets and assert their combined available memory.\n\nNote: If this suggestion does",
            "automated": true
          },
          {
            "token": "review-comment:4459852548:2026-11-03T20:06:18Z:",
            "type": "review-comment",
            "source": "https://github.com/kunchenguid/firstmate/pull/8135#discussion_r4459852548",
            "head": "3515632b0b5795f0d8d821c5e6133f24af564992",
            "author": "greptile-apps[bot]",
            "body": "<a href=\"#\"><img alt=\"P2\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\"></a> **Shared timeout goes untested**\n\nThe slow-command test sleeps before the first command, so it never checks that later commands share the remaining budget. Giving each command a fresh 350 ms timeout would still pass. Add staggered delays that exhaust the combined budget, plus a swap-only timeout case that keeps the measured RAM and its verdict.\n\nNote: If this suggestion doesn't matc",
            "automated": true
          }
